<title>PANAMA: SOCCER-PANAMA AND EL SALVADOR DRAW 1-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</title>
<headline>SOCCER-PANAMA AND EL SALVADOR DRAW 1-1 IN WORLD CUP QUALIFIER.</headline>
<dateline>PANAMA CITY 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Panama and El Salvador drew</p>
<p>1-1 (halftime 1-0) in a CONCACAF semifinal stage group two World</p>
<p>Cup qualifying match played on Sunday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Panama - Juan Carlos Cubillas (45th minute)</p>
<p>El Salvador - Raul Diaz Arce (52nd)</p>
<p>Attendance: 10,000</p>
<p>Standings (tabulate under played, won, drawn, lost, goals</p>
<p>for, goals against, points)</p>
<p>Group one (after Sunday's match between Trinidad and</p>
<p>Guatemala</p>
<p> Costa Rica    1  1  0  0  1  0  3</p>
<p> Guatemala     1  0  1  0  1  1  1</p>
<p> Trinidad	2  0  1  1  1  2  1</p>
<p>United States 0  0  0  0  0  0  0</p>
<p>    Next match: Oct 16 - Guatemala v Costa Rica   </p>
<p>Group two</p>
<p> El Salvador   2  1  1  0  6  1  4</p>
<p> Canada	  1  1  0  0  3  1  3</p>
<p> Cuba	    2  1  0  1  3  6  3</p>
<p> Panama	  3  0  1  2  3  7  1</p>
<p>Next match: Oct 10 - Canada v Cuba</p>
<p>Group three</p>
<p> Jamaica	 2  2  0  0  5  1  6</p>
<p> Mexico	  2  1  0  1  4  2  3</p>
<p> Honduras	2  1  0  1  2  4  3</p>
<p> St. Vincent   2  0  0  2  1  5  0</p>
<p>Next match: Oct 13 - St Vincent v Honduras</p>
<p>Note: top two teams in each group qualify for the final</p>
<p>qualifying round.</p>
</text>
